<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57972" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίσις</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ,
		ʽκλίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bending,
				inclination</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραχήλου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pyrrh.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			; <i>sinking</i> of the sun, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				1095
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτίνων ἰθεῖαν κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					585
				</span></i>
			; <i>bend</i> of a river or tunnel, <i><span class="en">
				Agatharch.
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>lying down</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρθρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					114
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <i>place for lying on</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαλακὴ κ. ὕπνον ἑλέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					1.25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλισία</span>
			 IV, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.77
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Ren.Ves.</u>
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>turning</i>, of soldiers, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δόρυ
				ποιεῖσθαι τὴν κ.</span> to the right, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ἡνίαν</span> (or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀσπίδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			) to the left, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.115.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.23.2
			</span></i>, etc.; expld. as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κατ᾽ ἄνδρα κίνησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ascl.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					10.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>region, dime</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				615
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			<i>inflexion</i> of nouns and verbs, <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				632.8
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				12.14
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ κατὰ πρόσωπον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					130.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>augment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				23.53
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
